"""
Markdown after CommonMark, as a tree (AST, abstract syntax tree) and as HTML
(HyperText Markup Language) that always passes the sanitizer of
Standard.Html and so can be put into a page without a further check.

Blocks: headings (ATX, after the atx format of Aaron Swartz, with #, and
Setext with = or - below), paragraphs, thematic breaks, quotes and lists
(bulleted and ordered, nested in any way), indented code blocks and code
fences (with ``` or ~~~) with a language, tables of GFM (GitHub Flavored
Markdown) with alignment, task lists of GFM (- [ ] and - [x], as
class="task" and class="task done" on the li, without a box, as the
sanitizer drops input), link definitions.  Inline: emphasis (*, _, ** and
__), strikethrough of GFM (~~, as del; a single ~ stays text and is free
for subscript), code, links (inline, by reference, as an autolink in angle
brackets), images, hard and soft breaks, backslash escapes and entities.

Only what is harmless is set: raw HTML is not passed on but shown as text,
every <, >, &, " and ' appears as an entity.  Only parseMarkdownWithHtml
and markdownWithHtmlToHtml read raw HTML (HTML blocks and inline HTML after
CommonMark) and pass it on; then the whole HTML goes through sanitize with
richPolicy, which removes script, style, iframe, forms, attributes starting
with on and URLs with javascript:.  A link or an image is made only for a
URL (Uniform Resource Locator) with https://, http://, mailto:, a single /
or #, without blanks, control characters, backslash and any of < > " ';
every other URL stays as text.  Then the HTML goes through sanitize of
Standard.Html, even though the output is safe already: two layers.

The tree lies in a table of nodes; node 0 is the document.  The relatives of
a node come from firstChild, nextSibling and parentOf, 0 meaning none.  The
texts of the nodes lie in the tree and are read as views into it.

Limits: raw HTML only with the functions WithHtml, otherwise it appears as
text; there the sanitizer is the only layer for the raw HTML, and where it
reads otherwise than a browser, its reading holds: an open script without an
end takes the rest of the page, a processing instruction and a CDATA section
end for it at the first >, <!--> opens a comment up to the next -->, of the
named entities in attributes it knows six.  An HTML block in a quote or an
item can take a following line without a marker as a lazy continuation, as a
paragraph does.  Footnotes, anchors, callouts and [toc] only with
parseMarkdownWith and extended; no strikethrough with a single ~, no
autolinks without angle brackets.  A link, an image or a definition with a
URL outside the rule above (relative without /, empty, with a blank or a
backslash, another scheme) stays text, also where the CommonMark
specification makes a link.  Of the named entities the module knows those of
Latin-1 and 61 more, every other stays text; labels are brought to lower
case only character by character, for ASCII (American Standard Code for
Information Interchange), Latin-1, Latin Extended-A, Greek and Cyrillic
(the capital sharp s does not become SS).  Emphasis tells the Unicode
character classes apart only approximately.  Quotes and lists are nested at
most mostMarkdownDepth levels deep, what lies deeper is paragraph text; the
sanitizer lets at most 100 elements stand inside each other and drops deeper
tags, keeping their text.

    let tree: Tree := parseMarkdown("# Title\n\n- one\n- two\n");
    let kind: NodeKind := nodeKind(&tree, firstChild(&tree, 0));
    let html: String := treeToHtml(&tree);
    let direct: String := markdownToHtml("*Hello*");
"""
import Standard.String (
    String
);
import Standard.Html (
    Policy
);

module Wolly.Markdown is
    """
    What a node is.  Blocks: DocumentNode, ParagraphNode, HeadingNode,
    ThematicBreakNode, BlockQuoteNode, BulletListNode, OrderedListNode,
    ItemNode, CodeBlockNode, TableNode, TableRowNode, TableCellNode,
    DefinitionNode.  Inline: TextNode, SoftBreakNode, HardBreakNode,
    CodeSpanNode, EmphasisNode, StrongNode, LinkNode, ImageNode,
    StrikeNode (strikethrough of GFM).  Only in a tree of
    parseMarkdownWithHtml: HtmlBlockNode (a block) and HtmlInlineNode (in
    the text), raw HTML.  Only in a tree of parseMarkdownWith with
    extended: FootnoteNode (the definition of a footnote, its blocks as
    children), FootnoteRefNode (the reference [^label] in the text) and
    TocNode (a paragraph [toc], the table of contents).
    """
    union NodeKind: Free is
        case DocumentNode;
        case ParagraphNode;
        case HeadingNode;
        case ThematicBreakNode;
        case BlockQuoteNode;
        case BulletListNode;
        case OrderedListNode;
        case ItemNode;
        case CodeBlockNode;
        case TableNode;
        case TableRowNode;
        case TableCellNode;
        case DefinitionNode;
        case TextNode;
        case SoftBreakNode;
        case HardBreakNode;
        case CodeSpanNode;
        case EmphasisNode;
        case StrongNode;
        case LinkNode;
        case ImageNode;
        case StrikeNode;
        case HtmlBlockNode;
        case HtmlInlineNode;
        case FootnoteNode;
        case FootnoteRefNode;
        case TocNode;
    end;

    """
    The tree of a Markdown text.  Linear: destroyTree gives it back.
    """
    type Tree: Linear;

    """
    The most bytes parseMarkdown reads: 1048576.  A longer text is cut
    there; what is shown is the caller's decision.
    """
    function mostMarkdownBytes(): Index
        ensures result = 1048576;

    """
    The greatest depth to which quotes and lists are read inside each other:
    16.  What lies deeper is paragraph text.
    """
    function mostMarkdownDepth(): Index
        ensures result = 16;

    """
    The most link definitions a tree keeps: 512.  Further ones are read and
    dropped.
    """
    function mostDefinitions(): Index
        ensures result = 512;

    """
    The most headings that get an anchor in a tree of parseMarkdownWith with
    extended: 1024.  Later ones stay without.
    """
    function mostAnchors(): Index
        ensures result = 1024;

    """
    The tree of text.  The first mostMarkdownBytes bytes are read.  No text
    is an error: every sequence of bytes gives a tree, at least the
    document.
    """
    generic [T: Region]
    function parseMarkdown(text: Span[Nat8, T]): Tree
        ensures nodeCount(&result) >= 1;

    """
    The tree of text as with parseMarkdown, but with raw HTML: HTML blocks
    after CommonMark 0.31.2, section 4.6 (all seven kinds), as
    HtmlBlockNode and inline HTML after section 6.6 (opening and closing
    tags, comments, processing instructions, declarations, CDATA) as
    HtmlInlineNode; their nodeText is the source as it stands.  treeToHtml
    passes it on unchanged and then leads the whole HTML through sanitize
    with richPolicy.  Only for text whose author may write HTML: the
    sanitizer stays the only layer for the raw HTML.
    """
    generic [T: Region]
    function parseMarkdownWithHtml(text: Span[Nat8, T]): Tree
        ensures nodeCount(&result) >= 1;

    """
    The tree of text, with raw HTML as parseMarkdownWithHtml when html
    holds, otherwise as parseMarkdown.  With extended in addition, for the
    editor Canela and for Lucy: every heading gets an anchor as nodeInfo
    (h- and its text in lower case letters, digits and hyphens, the German
    umlauts and sharp s as ae oe ue ss, on a clash -2, -3 and on), a link #x
    points to the anchor h- and the word of x, a definition [^label]: text
    at the start of a block becomes a FootnoteNode, [^label] in the text a
    FootnoteRefNode, a paragraph [toc] a TocNode, and a quote whose first
    line is [!NOTE], [!TIP], [!IMPORTANT], [!WARNING] or [!CAUTION] a
    callout of that kind (nodeNumber 1 to 5; the line leaves the tree).
    treeToHtml then gives the headings an id, the callouts a div of the
    classes callout and callout-note and so on, and appends the footnotes
    the text refers to as a div of the class footnotes.
    """
    generic [T: Region]
    function parseMarkdownWith(text: Span[Nat8, T], html: Bool, extended: Bool): Tree
        ensures nodeCount(&result) >= 1;

    """
    Gives the tree back.
    No contract: it only frees or closes what it is given.
    """
    function destroyTree(tree: Tree): Unit;

    """
    How many nodes the tree has, the document (node 0) counted.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function nodeCount(tree: &[Tree, R]): Index
        ensures result >= 1;

    """
    The kind of the node n.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function nodeKind(tree: &[Tree, R], n: Index): NodeKind
        requires n < nodeCount(tree);

    """
    The first child of the node n, 0 when it has none.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function firstChild(tree: &[Tree, R], n: Index): Index
        requires n < nodeCount(tree)
        ensures result < nodeCount(tree);

    """
    The last child of the node n, 0 when it has none.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function lastChild(tree: &[Tree, R], n: Index): Index
        requires n < nodeCount(tree)
        ensures result < nodeCount(tree);

    """
    The next node under the same parent, 0 when n is the last.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function nextSibling(tree: &[Tree, R], n: Index): Index
        requires n < nodeCount(tree)
        ensures result < nodeCount(tree);

    """
    The parent of n; 0 for the document.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function parentOf(tree: &[Tree, R], n: Index): Index
        requires n < nodeCount(tree)
        ensures result < nodeCount(tree);

    """
    The text of the node n: the text of a TextNode, the content of a
    CodeSpanNode and of a CodeBlockNode, the target of a LinkNode and of an
    ImageNode, the label of a DefinitionNode in the form labels are compared
    in (white space folded, lower case), the source of an HtmlBlockNode
    (every line with its line end) and of an HtmlInlineNode.  Empty for
    every other node, also for paragraph and heading: their text lies in
    their children.
    There is no ensures: the length of the view follows the text, no
    property under O(1) but the type.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function nodeText(tree: &[Tree, R], n: Index): Span[Nat8, R]
        requires n < nodeCount(tree);

    """
    The second text of the node n: the title of a LinkNode and of an
    ImageNode, the info string of a CodeBlockNode (such as "rust ignore"),
    the target of a DefinitionNode (its title is its child, a TextNode),
    the anchor of a heading in a tree of parseMarkdownWith with extended,
    the label of a FootnoteNode in the form labels are compared in.  Empty
    for every other node.
    There is no ensures: the length of the view follows the text, no
    property under O(1) but the type.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function nodeInfo(tree: &[Tree, R], n: Index): Span[Nat8, R]
        requires n < nodeCount(tree);

    """
    A number of the node n: the level of a heading (1 to 6), the start
    number of an ordered list, the count of columns of a table, the
    alignment of a cell (0 none, 1 left, 2 centre, 3 right), 1 for the
    header row of a table, for an ItemNode the task of GFM (0 none, 1 open
    with [ ], 2 done with [x] or [X]), the number of a footnote for a
    FootnoteNode (0 when no reference names it) and a FootnoteRefNode, the
    kind of a callout for a BlockQuoteNode (0 none, 1 note, 2 tip,
    3 important, 4 warning, 5 caution), the count of footnotes with a
    reference for the document.  0 for every other node.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function nodeNumber(tree: &[Tree, R], n: Index): Index
        requires n < nodeCount(tree);

    """
    Whether the list n is tight: no blank line between its items and
    between the blocks of an item.  False for every other node.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function isTightList(tree: &[Tree, R], n: Index): Bool
        requires n < nodeCount(tree);

    """
    The rules of the sanitizer for the HTML of this module: the elements
    a blockquote br code del em h1 to h6 hr img li ol p pre strong table tbody
    td th thead tr ul and the attributes href title src alt class start.
    Links get rel="nofollow noopener".
    No contract: a value of its own type built from constants; no property cheaper than its type holds.
    """
    function markdownPolicy(): Policy;

    """
    The rules of the sanitizer for a tree with raw HTML: the elements of
    markdownPolicy and in addition abbr del div ins kbd mark s small span
    sub sup u, the attributes of markdownPolicy and in addition lang dir
    width height colspan rowspan.  Links get rel="nofollow noopener".  What
    the sanitizer never lets through stays out: script, style, iframe,
    forms and input, attributes starting with on, URLs with javascript: and
    any scheme other than http, https and mailto.
    No contract: a value of its own type built from constants; no property cheaper than its type holds.
    """
    function richPolicy(): Policy;

    """
    The HTML of the tree, led through the sanitizer of Standard.Html: with
    richPolicy for a tree of parseMarkdownWithHtml, otherwise with
    markdownPolicy.
    No contract: a text whose length follows the tree.
    """
    generic [R: Region]
    function treeToHtml(tree: &[Tree, R]): String;

    """
    text, Markdown, as HTML: parseMarkdown, treeToHtml and destroyTree in
    one.  The first mostMarkdownBytes bytes are read.
    No contract: a text whose length follows the text of the input.
    """
    generic [T: Region]
    function markdownToHtml(text: Span[Nat8, T]): String;

    """
    text, Markdown with raw HTML, as HTML: parseMarkdownWithHtml,
    treeToHtml (with richPolicy) and destroyTree in one.  The first
    mostMarkdownBytes bytes are read.
    No contract: a text whose length follows the text of the input.
    """
    generic [T: Region]
    function markdownWithHtmlToHtml(text: Span[Nat8, T]): String;

    """
    text as HTML: parseMarkdownWith with html and extended, treeToHtml and
    destroyTree in one.  With extended the HTML goes through the sanitizer
    with the elements of markdownPolicy or richPolicy, in addition div and
    sup, and the attribute id, which it keeps only as an anchor.
    No contract: a text whose length follows the text of the input.
    """
    generic [T: Region]
    function markdownToHtmlWith(text: Span[Nat8, T], html: Bool, extended: Bool): String;

    """
    Whether url may be the target of a link: see the description of the
    module.
    No contract: a run over url whose cost grows with its length.
    """
    generic [U: Region]
    function isSafeLink(url: Span[Nat8, U]): Bool;
end module.
